    "body": "## Security impact\n\nREST authentication already treats the JWT `av` claim as part of the access identity: after a password reset or other credential invalidation increments `User.authVersion`, old access tokens immediately stop authenticating.\n\nSTOMP/WebSocket `CONNECT` did not enforce that same invariant. It parsed the token only far enough to recover the email, reloaded an ACTIVE user, and established a WebSocket principal without comparing the token's `av` claim to the user's current `authVersion`. An access token issued before a password reset could therefore establish a new authenticated WebSocket session until the token itself expired, even while the same token already received `401` on REST.\n\n## Fix\n\n- parse the full `JwtUtil.AccessTokenIdentity` during STOMP `CONNECT`;\n- reload the ACTIVE user as before;\n- reject the connection unless `identity.authVersion() == user.getAuthVersion()`;\n- establish the WebSocket principal only after that comparison succeeds;\n- leave SEND denial, subscription authorization, roles, ACTIVE-user checks, chat/tracking membership checks and rate limiting unchanged.\n\nThis PR closes the stale-token **reconnect** path. It does not claim to actively evict a WebSocket session that was already authenticated before an auth-version change; active session eviction/credential-bound session TTL is a separate lifecycle hardening concern.\n\n## Tests\n\n- unit coverage proves a matching auth version establishes the STOMP principal;\n- unit coverage proves a stale auth version is rejected with `BadCredentialsException`;\n- a stdlib-only raw WebSocket/STOMP runtime probe establishes a real `CONNECTED` session without adding test-only API endpoints or external Python dependencies;\n- the existing password-recovery smoke now proves the complete credential-invalidation contract:\n  1. the pre-reset access token can STOMP CONNECT;\n  2. password reset increments `auth_version` and the same token is rejected by REST;\n  3. the same stale token is rejected on a new STOMP CONNECT;\n  4. a fresh access token after login can STOMP CONNECT again.\n\n## Merge gate\n\nMerge only after all relevant checks on the exact PR head SHA are green. Revalidate the exact head, review threads and current `master` immediately before merge. If `master` moves, integrate it and rerun exact-head checks. Merge with a merge commit guarded by the checked head SHA, then verify merge parents and every post-merge push workflow before starting another slice.",
